 "poem": "Or a lingering heave of breathing,\nOr the shafts that flit in vibration,\nAnd the sharp echo heard around,\nOr the deep, writhing relaxation,\nOf the four lower souls at entire;\nBut no sound is confirmation\nFrom above, but only silence;\nFor the world's soul no time exists can\nIn the time of its coming death.\nOne alone may say, \"Here I meditate,\n\"By its own strength.\" But alone\nShe sits and meditates. Fate",
